on american artifacts only on american  history tv  produced by the japanese committee for  the investigation of u.s war crimes in  vietnam testimony of truth was filmed  between december 1966 and january of  1967 and details civilian injuries and  deaths caused by u.s bombing in north  vietnam  the documentary debuted in may of 1967  at the bertrand russell international  war crimes tribunal in stockholm sweden  and comes to us courtesy of the  swarthmore college peace collection  it contains graphic scenes of war that  some viewers may find disturbing  on march the 16th 1965 in a street in  detroit michigan mrs ellis hers then 82  years old a nazi refugee and a  peace-loving quaker  turned herself into a blazing human  torch in protest of the united states  war in vietnam  in her final not accusing lyndon b  johnson before the creator of this world  she appealed as follows to the nations  of the world and the american people  awake and take action before it is too  late  yours is a responsibility to decide if  this world shall be a good place to live  for all human beings in dignity and  peace  or if it should blow itself up to  oblivion god is not marked  professor shingo shibata at jose  university tokyo who since 1952 had been  corresponding with her was one of those  to whom she addressed her final note  he was deeply moved by the depth of her  concern and her act of self-sacrifice  this led him to compile a collection of  her letters to him and the book was  published under the title phoenix  letters for peace  in japan the story of alice hearst and  the book were given a wide publicity  throughout japan  by the royalties on the book he founded  the peace fund in memory of mrs hurst  with a purpose to help the wall stricken  vietnamese people  and the ethnic victims of hiroshima and  nagasaki because if he felt this would  be the best way to correspond to the  wish of the late mrs hers  this film which was shown as a document  of the united states war crimes in  vietnam in the bertrand russell  international tribunal  held in stockholm from may the 2nd  through the 10th 1967  is presented as a gift by the alice  hearst peace fund to the people of other  countries including american people and  we hope  that this film will be helpful for your  work toward peace let us work ever  harder to fulfill the last wish of mrs  hearst so that there will be no war on  the earth but peace  the atrocities being committed by  america against the vietnamese people  have steadily grown worse  continuous air raids are now going on  against the democratic republic of  vietnam  at the beginning of 1966 bertrand  russell the british philosopher  proposed that an international war  crimes tribune will be organized in the  name of freedom and social justice and  based on international law  the war crimes committed in vietnam  should be judged by the conscience of  the world says earl russell  [Music]  in support of this appeal a japanese  committee for the investigation of war  crimes in vietnam was established in  october the same year  [Music]  last december  a team consisting of seven members was  sent to the democratic republic of  vietnam from japan  the team of investigators began their  examination of american war crimes in  vietnam walking by foot and seeing with  their own eyes  [Music]  we arrived in hanoi on december the 21st  two days before the christmas cease fire  mister farm got dark  chairman of the committee of the  democratic republic of vietnam for the  investigation of war crimes  and also minister of health and hygiene  colonel harvan low  vice chairman farm von buck he is also  chief justice of the supreme court  after making detailed arrangements on  objects methods and schedule of the  investigation  we started our on the spot survey  dividing the work between us  we started from hanoi to the south along  highway number one  by way of vin dong hoy and gutoy  our team first went down near to the  17th parallel  we then carried on our investigations in  tang ho  [Music]  and the city of hanoi  we drove more than two thousand miles  over twenty seven days  talked directly with more than two  hundred witnesses  and collected a great variety of  material evidence  bombing by the americans is mainly on  such non-military targets as densely  populated districts in villages and  cities  the city of vin the capital of the  gayang province  this is a place of total destruction not  even the features of this former  industrial center can be found  even the building of the international  control commission for supervision of  cessation of hostilities established on  the geneva agreements was bombed  [Music]  churches are no exception  [Music]  about 1 000 tons of bombs have been  dropped here in more than 63 air raids  this was the city of dong hoy the  capital of kuang bin province  this commercial town in central vietnam  which lies 40 miles from the 17th  parallel has been reduced to rubble  [Music]  their targets are only military  as you can see their aim is to destroy  our production and wipe us out  this was the city of donghui it has been  bombed  390 times continuing until today  it started when the air raids on the  north began on february the 7th 1965  hanoi the capital city of the democratic  republic of vietnam  this is how the residential district and  school buildings look now at the central  part of the city  [Music]  this gives the complete lie  to the united states administration's  claim that they refrain from bombing  non-military targets in hanoi  the facts are evident  [Music]  the city of haifang  this largest commercial city in the  delta of the songkoi river  has also been systematically destroyed  everywhere by raids with missiles and  rockets  the city of naam din  this was the center of the textile  industry it is now virtually in ruins  [Music]  only the monument on a street corner  shows that workers and their families  once were living here  many educational facilities have been  bombed by the united states  more than 120 schools have been  destroyed up till now  this is all that remains of the middle  school  in trident  one of the school boys says  air aids have destroyed all the school  buildings  we had sheltered in the dugout below the  passage but were all buried and narrowly  escaped death and crept out again  one woman teacher and 12 pupils across  the passage were killed  it was about nine o'clock in the morning  of july the 18th  an air raid began just as i came home  from school and i rushed out of the room  in a hurry  feeling uneasy about my father i was  running to the farm when down came a  bomb and i was knocked to the ground i  remember nothing else  because i felt unconscious  [Music]  she says  before the raids i used to come home  from school very happy with all my folks  father mother grandfather and  grandmother  but all 13 of them including an unborn  baby have been killed  only i am left  even little babies are innocent victims  of these american air raids  [Music]  america has systematically attacked  hospitals  in tying her and to the south in  particular they have bombed all  provincial and prefectural hospitals  this is the site of the former k-71  tuberculosis hospital in tangho province  there were some 50 buildings here  all are now destroyed  [Music]  thirty people including five doctors  were killed and many others wounded  [Music]  this donghoi hospital was the object of  an attack when the city of dong hoy was  first bombed in 1965  it has been bombed 13 times since then  raids have continued until now it has  ceased to function  [Music]  this nurse  miss huang tilly  injured by a bomb while she was  preparing for an operation  said  americans say that only military targets  are bombed  this is a downright lie  about a quarter past seven on the  morning of september the 11th 1965  there was the droning of a plane in the  southwest  bang went to bomb and i was knocked down  dizzy  what i will never forget is that the  doctor tried to continue his operation  although he himself had been  badly wounded  so that his innards  could almost be seen  mrs leon one of my fellow nurses had her  head split open and died  two children of hers are left orphans  americans have smashed our happy life  our indignation is beyond descriptions  who has lost one of his arms says  i was blown over by a bomb blast while  waiting for my brother for treatment  that day  coming to myself i found one of my arms  gone  and my brother had been killed there  the hospital building was clearly marked  with a large red cross  its destruction could not have been by  mistake  in carrying on their criminal war of  mass destruction  america is using supersonic jet planes  of the latest type  but above all they are using the most  criminal weapons of extermination  anti-personnel bombs forbidden by  international law  we collected and examined different  kinds of weapons in the bond areas  the chemicals used include yellow  phosphor poison gases herbicides and  defoliators  mr fan  tween  chairman of the committee for  investigation of war crimes of kwang bin  province showed that america is making  vietnam  a proving ground for their new weapons  in this kwangbin province including the  demilitarized zone on the 17th parallel  a machine gun ball  the fuse of an a palm bomb  a fuse from a cbu  the palm cinders scraped off the wall of  dong hoy hospital  as part of their strategy us planes  dropped transistor radios on both the  case and on its dry cells the name of  hitachi of japan can be read  forged money  pencils ballpoint pens and erasers were  dropped for the same purpose  tombow  ball ballpoint pen  made in japan  here we see a pineapple bomb  manufactured specifically for the  extermination of people  it weighs 20 pounds  when dropped its flanges open and it  explodes on touching the ground  on detonation  about 250 small steel pellets are  scattered and kill everything within 50  feet  this is the ball bomb  the canister bomb unit or cbu  it is the latest type  an improvement on the pineapple bomb  more effective for killing and maiming  it weighs about a pound  300 small steel pellets are in its shell  these kill over a range of 10 meters  the board explodes on landing  the parent bomb carrying these  holds the 300 to 600 small bombs  it separates into two pieces while  falling  and ball bombs scatter over a wide area  covering about six hundred feet  and three thousand feet in the direction  of flight  the ball bomb cannot destroy military  facilities  it is a weapon designed solely for the  purpose of mass murder  in the company of the international  investigation team sent by bertrand  russell  we listened to the victims of ball bombs  in the city of vignene  four children of mrs  vin t ray who stayed at home  were killed  an iron kettle and a vacuum bottle  riddled with steel pellets  this city of vinyen was the testing  ground for the mass use of these ball  bombs  the penetration of a steel pellet is  enough for a single shot to prove fatal  although the wound is small the pellet  causes complex injury inside the body  it can be found only by x-ray  it is impossible for mass-produced  victims to be treated quickly  this shows the back of a victim who  received  ball bomb wounds all over his body  here we see a patient undergoing  surgical treatment  the dark dots on these fingers are  caused by a cbu bomb  there is no doubt  that the ball bomb is a weapon of mass  destruction strictly forbidden by  international law  in the rural areas of binyan city  we were able to confirm the mass use of  ball bombs and their vast spread of  destruction  the white marks on the field show where  each of the ball bombs fell  here we see the countless shot holes  made by small steel pellets on the  farmhouse wall  the donghoy hospital was attacked 13  times with napalm bombs forbidden by  international law  we confirmed the use of napalm bombs by  the cinders on the wall of the hospital  and we brought some of these back with  us  now palm burns with terrific heat of  more than one thousand degrees  centigrade and the death rate from it is  very high  now the even more terrible supernatant  is being used  that is napalm mixed with yellow  phosphorus  the poison of yellow phosphorus  penetrates the skin  and causes deadly functional disorders  these keloid scars of napalm are no  different from those suffered by the  hiroshima victims of the united states  atom bomb  a victim of napalm in south vietnam  this man's arm not only has keloids but  is actually welded to his body  the mission of the national front for  liberation of south vietnam in hanoi  mr gwen van tien  head of the mission talks about the  present situation in south vietnam  american imperialists and their puppet  government are guilty of every kind of  war crime  such as  scorched earth operation chemical  warfare forced concentration of the  inhabitants into so-called strategic  hamlets experiments with new types of  death weapons and so on  here is the evidence  [Music]  she is a victim of american aggression  in the south and is now receiving  medical treatment in the north she says  when i was 18 i was arrested three times  and cruelly tortured for three years for  no other reason than that i was for a  united election as stipulated in the  geneva agreements  finally i was thrown out as a corpse in  the field  before i went to prison i weighed 256  pounds but when i was thrown out my  weight was only 122 pounds  it is now seven years since then but  both inside and outside of my body i am  covered with injuries  in prison there uh were some 240 people  only 14 of whom have survived  america has bombed dams dikes channels  and other irrigation facilities and is  trying to massacre the people by floods  and by destroying agriculture  they are doing saturation bombing of  dikes and irrigation facilities in the  delta zones where there is dense  population and good crops  even small canals and water controls  used for irrigation have been attacked  with rockets  there are no military facilities in the  neighborhood of dykes so destroyed  the fact that such raids are carried out  during the rainy season confirms the  real intentions of the american  imperialists  even farm houses standing here and there  in rice fields have not been excluded  from bombing attacks  in this house a family of parents and  the child were killed instantly by  sitting at table  [Music]  the school child of a farmer living in  the next house was also killed  [Music]  mrs chan the wei  at the same village tells about her four  children who were killed before her eyes  how sad i am  i was robbed of my husband without a  single word  my only child left also died  against the americans who have destroyed  this happiness  i will fight till there is not a single  american in vietnam  i hope you will make this cruelty of  america known to all the people of the  world  [Music]  in memory of her youngest child she  asked us to present it to japanese  mothers as a memento  this orphan boy named bong told us that  his mother  elder brother and younger sister were  all killed instantly and then he said  i want to study hard and train myself  and i will fight the americans to the  last  i hope japanese boys and girls will also  fight hand in hand with us vietnamese  my name don't get high  and back  um  this is gertruity  formerly a fishing village lying 13  miles from the 17th parallel  here americans first destroyed all the  houses with bombs and napalm  then cutting off the retreat of the  people they dropped a great number of  anti-personnel pineapple bombs  this was calculated mass murder  [Music]  in this way  three hamlets of good terry village were  completely wiped off the map  [Music]  we had an interview with an american  pilot held as a prisoner of war  lieutenant commander charles n tanner  from the aircraft carrier coral sea  which uses yokosuka japan as its base  what were the tactics you used in your  bombing attacks  other tactics  was  to  circle the town  uh with fragmentation bombs so as to  drive the people  into their air raid shelters in the  middle of the town  then as the people went into their  air raid shelters then  another pass was made  dropped napalm to burn them out of the  shelters  as they ran from the shelters out of the  town and then  cbu was dropped on the outskirts of town  to achieve total annihilation  could you distinguish between military  and non-military targets yes we studied  reconnaissance  in uh  [Music]  in most cases you can distinguish  what was your purpose yes  foodie was attacked for that purpose and  that aim  to demoralize the people  so they would put pressure upon their  government  to force a compromise to peacetime  president ho chi minh of the democratic  republic of vietnam  together with the international  investigation team we met president hull  severely condemning america for its war  crimes against the vietnamese people  premier fan von dong emphasized that  there cannot be peace in vietnam without  independence and unity for the people of  all vietnam  while in hanoi we held two press  interviews  deputy leader of the group mr ishijima  speaks  from what i have seen with my own eyes  and touched with my own hands i assert  on full responsibility of what the  united states administration says is a  lie  totally contrary  my impression and firm conviction is  that america is using the vietnamese  people as guinea pigs on whom they are  testing their new weapons  harrison salisbury of the new york times  wilfred burchett a famous australian  journalist  [Music]  the statement issued by the japanese  investigation team says  these acts by the united states clearly  constitute a crime of aggression against  the democratic republic of vietnam  a crime against peace and against  humanity the crime of the use of  unlawful and inhumane weapons poison  gases and chemical weapons which are  forbidden by international law  the crime of attack on non-military  targets and non-combatants and so on  [Music]  we earnestly hope that the results of  our investigations into these criminal  acts will make a contribution to ending  america's crimes and to winning a great  victory for vietnam and for independence  freedom and peace for the vietnamese  people  [Music]  you can watch archival films on public  affairs in their entirety on our weekly  series real america saturday at 10 pm  and sunday at 4 pm eastern here on  american history tv  sunday on book

