se  population and good crops  even small canals and water controls  used for irrigation have been attacked  with rockets  there are no military facilities in the  neighborhood of dykes so destroyed  the fact that such raids are carried out  during the rainy season confirms the  real intentions of the american  imperialists  even farm houses standing here and there  in rice fields have not been excluded  from bombing attacks  in this house a family of parents and  the child were killed instantly by  sitting at table  [Music]  the school child of a farmer living in  the next house was also killed  [Music]  mrs chan the wei  at the same village tells about her four  children who were killed before her eyes  how sad i am  i was robbed of my husband without a  single word  my only child left also died  against the americans who have destroyed  this happiness  i will fight till there is not a single  american in vietnam  i hope you will make this cruelty of  america known to all the people of the  world  [Music]  in memory of her youngest child she  asked us to present it to japanese  mothers as a memento  this orphan boy named bong told us that  his mother  elder brother and younger sister were  all killed instantly and then he said  i want to study hard and train myself  and i will fight the americans to the  last  i hope japanese boys and girls will also  fight hand in hand with us vietnamese  my name don't get high  and back  um  this is gertruity  formerly a fishing village lying 13  miles from the 17th parallel  here americans first destroyed all the  houses with bombs and napalm  then cutting off the retreat of the  people they dropped a great number of  anti-personnel pineapple bombs  this was calculated mass murder  [Music]  in this way  three hamlets of good terry village were  completely wiped off the map  [Music]  we had an interview with an american  pilot held as a prisoner of war  lieutenant commander charles n tanner  from the aircraft carrier coral sea  which uses yokosuka japan as its base  what were the tactics you used in your  bombing attacks  other tactics  was  to  circle the town  uh with fragmentation bombs so as to  drive the people  into their air raid shelters in the  middle of the town  then as the people went into their  air raid shelters then  another pass was made  dropped napalm to burn them out of the  shelters  as they ran from the shelters out of the  town and then  cbu was dropped on the outskirts of town  to achieve total annihilation  could you distinguish between military  and non-military targets yes we studied  reconnaissance  in uh  [Music]  in most cases you can distinguish  what was your purpose yes  foodie was attacked for that purpose and  that aim  to demoralize the people  so they would put pressure upon their  government  to force a compromise to peacetime  president ho chi minh of the democratic  republic of vietnam  together with the international  investigation team we met president hull  severely condemning america for its war  crimes against the vietnamese people  premier fan von dong emphasized that  there cannot be peace in vietnam without  independence and unity for the people of  all vietnam  while in hanoi we held two press  interviews  deputy leader of the group mr ishijima  speaks  from what i have seen with my own eyes  and touched with my own hands i assert  on full responsibility of what the  united states administration says is a  lie  totally contrary  my impression and firm conviction is  that america is using the vietnamese  people as guinea pigs on whom they are  testing their new weapons  harrison salisbury of the new york times  wilfred burchett a famous australian  journalist  [Music]  the statement issued by the japanese  investigation team says  these acts by the united states clearly  constitute a crime of aggression against  the democratic republic of vietnam  a crime against peace and against  humanity the crime of the use of  unlawful and inhumane weapons poison  gases and chemical weapons which are  forbidden by international law  the crime of attack on non-military  targets and non-combatants and so on  [Music]  we earnestly hope that the results of  our investigations into these criminal  acts will make a contribution to ending  america's crimes and to winning a great  victory for vietnam and for independence  freedom and peace for the vietnamese  people  [Music]  you can watch archival films on public  affairs in their entirety on our weekly  series real america saturday at 10 pm  and sunday at 4 pm eastern here on  american history tv  sunday on book
 

